  <!-- faq -->
  <section id="faq">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p>Short answers to the questions people ask most before installing microterm.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <aside class="faq-help">
        <span class="faq-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3M12 17h.01"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Still have a question?</h3>
        <p>Read the documentation, or open an issue on GitHub.</p>
        <div class="faq-links">
          <a class="chipbtn" href={`${base}/docs/installation/`}>Documentation</a>
          <a class="chipbtn" href="https://github.com/0funct0ry/microterm/issues">GitHub issues</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>Does microterm run on Windows?</summary>
          <p>No. microterm supports macOS and Linux only, so that behaviour stays consistent and native on both platforms.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to configure anything before using it?</summary>
          <p>No. microterm works with sensible defaults out of the box. When you want to change something, run <code>Open config</code> from the command palette.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where is the configuration file?</summary>
          <p>At <code>~/.config/microterm/microterm.toml</code>. Changes apply as soon as you save the file.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does microterm collect any data?</summary>
          <p>No. microterm has no telemetry and only connects to servers you configure, such as SSH hosts.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do I report a bug or request a feature?</summary>
          <p>Open an issue on GitHub. Include your operating system, microterm version, and steps to reproduce the problem.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

